Smart Enclosure Controller

An ongoing personal project to build a modular system for monitoring and managing environmental conditions in reptile, aquarium, and other small-pet enclosures.

The project uses an ESP32 to collect environmental data and communicates with a Raspberry Pi backend using MQTT. A desktop application is also being developed to provide a user interface for monitoring and controlling the system.

features
    Temperature and humidity monitoring using a DHT22 sensor
    ESP32-based sensor data collection
    MQTT communication between the ESP32 and Raspberry Pi
    Python backend running on a Raspberry Pi
    Initial desktop application built with PySide6
    Modular design intended to support additional sensors and automation (plug and play system)
    planned multiple enclosures (ESP32) being handles and attached to one rasbpi and shown on one desktop app



rough architecture

sensors -> esp32 -> MQTT -> raspi -> python and WebSocket -> desktop app


challanges
    Humidty:
        Humidty is unpredictable changes can pick up pace fast 
        having a system that adapts would still need time to calibrate and adjust creating a window where humidty is unstable

Gaoland focus:
    Back end communication, IoT, embedded systems and networking
    


This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
